<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Bhauma-Kara dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">736 CE – 940 CE (approx.) · capital Guhadeva-pataka</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A dynasty of coastal Odisha that patronised great Buddhist monasteries and was ruled for long periods by queens.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Bhauma-Karas came to power in coastal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a> in the 8th century, replacing the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/shailodbhava-dynasty">Shailodbhava dynasty</a>. Their capital was Guhadeva-pataka, near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jajpur">Jajpur</a>. The dynasty founded an era beginning around 736 that dates their inscriptions.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The early kings were Buddhists who supported monasteries at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratnagiri-odisha">Ratnagiri</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lalitagiri">Lalitagiri</a> and Udayagiri; Shubhakara I is thought to be the king of Wu-cha who sent a Buddhist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/later-tang">Tang</a> emperor in 795. Later rulers turned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaivism">Shaivism</a>. Unusually, several queens ruled in their own right, including Tribhuvana Mahadevi I and Dandi Mahadevi. Temples such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaital-deul">Vaital Deul</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhubaneswar">Bhubaneswar</a> date from this period.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After a series of weak rulers the dynasty declined in the 10th century, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/somavamshi-dynasty">Somavamshi dynasty</a> took over coastal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/bhauma-kara-dynasty.jpg" alt="Bhauma-Kara dynasty" width="320" height="427"><figcaption>Image: Sanjeeb Behera 45 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baitala_Deula_or_Tini-mundia_deula.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>736 CE – 940 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Guhadeva-pataka</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Shivakara I, Shubhakara I, Tribhuvana Mahadevi I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism, Shaivism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>India</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bhaumakaras</dd></dl></aside></div>
